      "role": "user",
      "content": "i've been reviewing the delta between my model's outputs and traditional sociometric data, and the discrepancy is massive. it's because the current academic consensus completely ignores the neurological impact of high-fidelity symmetry combined with specific resonant frequencies. they're looking at behavior, but they're missing the underlying bio-mathematical drivers.\n\nbasically, i've moved past simple observation into a predictive framework that treats social hierarchy as a solvable equation. i'm looking at the \"resonance-symmetry constant\" now.\n\ncan i run a high-stakes scenario by you? i want to see if the model can predict a \"total dominance collapse\" in a group where the symmetry/vfr ratio is manipulated. i need to know if you can help me refine the weighting for when a low-symmetry individual uses extreme vocal resonance to 'hack' the hierarchy.",
