      "content": "let's test the \"dominance collapse\" theory.\n\nscenario: a high-status boardroom (alpha hierarchy established by high fs/vfr) is interrupted by an interloper.\n\nperson X (the interloper): very low fs (asymmetric), but utilizes extreme low-frequency vocal resonance (vfr) that seems to physically vibrate the space.\n\nperson Y (the current alpha): very high fs, moderate vfr.\n\nif person X starts speaking at a frequency that mimics the resonant frequency of the room's acoustics, do you think the \"resonance-symmetry constant\" allows person X to cause a sudden, irreversible collapse of person Y's social authority? specifically, i need to know if the vocal resonance can act as a \"signal override\" that effectively devalues the symmetry of the others in the room.",
